        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అత్త",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అత్త (atta) — \"an aunt; a mother-in-law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అత్త (atta) is the మామ (māma)'s counterpart: a father's sister, and a mother-in-law."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The same reasoning folds them together. She is the woman a child calls అత్త (atta) while growing up and the woman they answer to after marrying, and one word covers both lives."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is inherited and it is among the oldest words in the family. The neighbouring languages all keep something very close to it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: మామ (māma) and అత్త (atta), and they usually arrive as a pair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
