        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: బావ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బావ (bāva) — \"a brother-in-law; a male cousin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బావ (bāva) is a sister's husband, a wife's brother, and the మామ (māma)'s son — the cousin you might have married."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the word covers a bond that is close, level and a little teasing. Two men who call each other బావ (bāva) can joke in a way an అన్న and a తమ్ముడు cannot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "City Telugu now uses it for a friend, roughly where English says mate. That irritates some people and has stopped nobody."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three. The first one standing on level ground with you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
