          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: మరదలు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మరదలు (maradalu) — \"a sister-in-law; a female cousin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మరదలు (maradalu) is the బావ (bāva)'s counterpart on the other side: a wife's younger sister, a younger brother's wife, and the మామ (māma)'s daughter — the cousin you might have married."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So it carries the same easy, teasing register that బావ (bāva) does. A బావ (bāva) and a మరదలు (maradalu) can joke across a room in a way an అన్న and a చెల్లి cannot, and Telugu films have lived off that for eighty years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is inherited, and it belongs to the same reckoning as the rest of this chapter: the person a marriage hands you was very often somebody the family already had a word for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. The one who matches బావ (bāva)."
            }
          ]
        },
