          "title": "You'll want to know: అల్లుడు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అల్లుడు (alluḍu) — \"a son-in-law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అల్లుడు (alluḍu) is a daughter's husband — the మామ (māma)'s word for the young man on the far side of the match."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "He is treated as a guest for life. An అల్లుడు (alluḍu) on a visit is fed first, seated first and asked after first, and the household's own people wait their turn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which is what the chapter has been building to: మామ (māma), అత్త (atta), బావ (bāva), మరదలు (maradalu), అల్లుడు (alluḍu). Ask each of them how they are and you have done the whole visit properly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: మామ (māma), అత్త (atta), బావ (bāva), మరదలు (maradalu), అల్లుడు (alluḍu). A marriage's worth of new people to ask after."
            }
          ]
